# THE EXPECTATION COMMIT IS 1 COMMIT BEHIND THE TREE (`git rev-list --count
# c16c3e9..0330b46`), and the artifact records both. **CORRECTED (D0A-R23-11): this said
# THREE, conflating three FIXES with three COMMITS — all three runner fixes landed in one
# commit, 0330b46.** That is the same fixes-versus-commits confusion R22-02 removed from this
# file's hand-written provenance, recurring in the sentence that describes the mechanism which
# replaced it. Counts belong to `git rev-list`, not to recollection.
# That is the property the protocol asserted from R21-07 onward and could not demonstrate:
# a reader who was not present can now check that the prediction predates the measurement,
# because the runner read a COMMITTED blob it could not have written and bound the pair into
# one artifact. The ONE commit between carries three runner fixes; none touched a Rust test,
# which is what the derivation predicted and why the figure holding is informative rather than
# merely unchanged.
